entry.summary:
You don't need Datadog, PagerDuty, or a $29/month plan to monitor your websites. With 40 lines of code and a free API, you can build uptime monitoring that actually alerts you when things break. Here's the complete setup. A script that: Checks if your websites are up every 5 minutes Takes a screenshot when something goes down (proof of the failure) Sends you an alert via webhook (Slack, Discord, or email) Logs response times so you can spot slow degradation Runs on any machine (VPS, Raspberry Pi, GitHub Actions) const https = require('https');
